# Code owners: a change to these paths needs their review, when branch protection on
# `main` requires a review from code owners (Settings -> Branches). The trust anchors are
# listed: a public key swapped here, or a release workflow changed, would let someone
# else's key sign licences or images that verify. Per the security review of 2026-10-27
# (H3, L30), so are every workflow and the deploy and build definitions: a workflow decides
# which job reads which secret and on which runner, and a Dockerfile or deploy script
# decides what the published images and assets contain. And the contracts everyone else
# builds on, CONVENTIONS.md, PLATFORM.md and the runner protocol's schemas, which anyone,
# agents included, may change in a pull request, so that every change to them passes their
# code owner.

# The licence's public keys (ADR-0077, decision 6): each trusted key id signs licences.
/ee/src/main/resources/ee/licence-public-keys/ @JiriBalcar
